EXT. ROOFTOP OF A DRAGON-SCALE TOWER, MOONLIT CLIFFTOP KINGDOM - NIGHT

Slate tiles glittering with frost. Chimneys leaking violet smoke. A gale from the sea.

Six figures crouch behind a stone gargoyle. A GLOWING STAFF-BEARER in a hooded cloak (WREN OYELARAN-THORNE, wizard, 30s) holds a staff that hums. SIR BRAM DELACROIX-ASANTE (40s, dented armor) grips a sword. A HALFLING THIEF, PIPPA SUMNER-NWOSU (20s, tiny, fingerless gloves), clings to the gargoyle's ear. A FOX-EARED BARD, JULIAN AKINTOLA-REYES (30s, lute strapped to his back), quivers. An old DWARVEN ENGINEER, GRUNHILDA KOWALSKI-BELL (60s, goggles, a beard braided with gears), peers over the ridge. And a small, silent FIGURE in rags, who has said nothing for three days.

WREN
(to the group)
On my signal. We cross the ridge, take the beacon, and we're out.

SIR BRAM
(to Pippa)
You're sure the locks are open?

PIPPA
(muttering)
Sure as sure can be.

JULIAN
(to himself)
I am too pretty to die on a roof.

GRUNHILDA
(to the group)
The wind will take the first one down. Hold your hats.

The silent figure steps forward, lowers its hood, and lifts the beacon from the parapet as easily as picking an apple. The gale dies. Sir Brram drops his sword. Pippa slips from the gargoyle. Julian's lute strings snap in unison. Wren's staff goes dark. Grunhilda tilts her goggles up.

GRUNHILDA (CONT'D)
That's not what I expected.

The figure turns, and under the hood is a girl of ten, eyes full of stars.

GIRL
It was always mine.

WREN
(slowly)
Starlight. The lost heir.

STARLIGHT
Call me home.
